      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "This dashboard is the **phase 5** proof of [todo/graph-wide-migration.md](https://github.com/grafana/grafana-echarts-panel):\neach mark answers for itself. Every panel runs the *same* row-format query \u2014 the plugin's\nregistered transformation converts it to `graph-nodes-wide` / `graph-edges-wide` above the\npanel, so each node and each edge exists as a field before overrides are applied.\n\n**Try it:**\n\n1. **Hover** a node, then an edge. Each value is formatted by that mark's own unit and decimals.\n2. **Click** a mark to pin its tooltip. Only the marks with a `links` override show a footer link.\n3. **Click a legend swatch** and pick a colour: Grafana writes a plain `byName` colour override \u2014\n   no plugin-specific mechanism \u2014 and the node repaints. **Click a legend label** to hide that node\n   and the edges touching it.\n4. Open **Field overrides** and look at the field picker: it lists `gateway`, `api`, `db`,\n   `gw-api`, `api-db`, `gw-db` \u2014 one entry per mark."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "Per-mark units \u2014 hover any node or edge",
      "description": "**One unit per mark, not one per frame.**\n\n`gateway` and `api` are milliseconds, `db` is a percentage, and each edge carries its own unit again (`gw-api` req/s, `api-db` seconds, `gw-db` percent). Node values are printed on the canvas too, through the same per-mark formatter \u2014 the label and the tooltip cannot disagree.\n\nBefore the field contract the tooltip formatted every mark with the frame's *first* numeric column, so the hovered item's unit depended on frame order.",
